      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Chronic pain and tenderness in the groin, labia majora, and medial thigh can be caused by neuropathy of the genitofemoral nerve. Differentiation from ilioinguinal neuralgia by diagnostic blocks is crucial to selecting proper treatment. Three women with genitofemoral neuralgia underwent laparoscopic examination and treatment, thus avoiding laparotomy and flank incision."},
